A||||3||fierolarry||water separator removal||||5||
Z||000000||fierolarry||03-15-2001||12:21 PM||||Anyone know an easy way to remove the water separator from an 87 GT.I want to make a ram air setup and intake kit.||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||03-15-2001||01:19 PM||||Its pretty straight forward after you take off the wheel well and the wheel. There are 2 10 mm (I think)bolts that are holding on to the seperator.  Once you have that out of the way it makes such a nice noise when accelerating...whoossssssh!<P>There are a couple aftermarket intake tubes out there I think, I know that Chris West just had a price reduction on his. I might go to that eventually, but what I did was take out the seperator, replaced it with 3 inch tubing and added on a Holley style intake scoop outside. <P>Its nice but I would love to make a RAM AIR version with Mecham Scoops! Also check in the archives there have been many threads about this very procedure if you haven't already.||||reg||6
Z||000002||ChadMan||03-15-2001||02:01 PM||||Be careful if you live in a damp area, like soggy Central Ohio for example.  The previous owner had removed the water separator from the 86 SE V6 I had and the air cleaner housing was full of rust and crap.<P>It did make a nice WHOOOOOSH on acceleration though!||||reg||4
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||03-15-2001||10:56 PM||||Rain can be a consideration, and though we don't get that much rain, or weather for that matter, in So California it isnt' that much of a problem for me. <P>However, the times that it has rained and rained hard to put your wipers on hi, I have not had any problem with water. Since you are going with Ram Air, more crap in the filter should be expected, the air intake is on a very dirty level of the road.||||reg||6
